(1.0 Overview of Factuality Evaluation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Factuality assessment is the process of verifying whether verifiable factual claims contained in AI model responses are true, supported by reliable evidence, or inaccurate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assessors must evaluate each checkable claim against high-quality, reputable external sources. Evaluations must distinguish verifiable claims from subjective opinions, pleasantries, and advice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.0 Identifying Claims) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A factual claim is a statement that asserts a verifiable fact about the real world, entities, dates, statistics, scientific principles, historical events, or geographical data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Checkable claims: 'The Denver Nuggets won the 2023 NBA Championship.') Tj T*
(- Subjective / non-checkable: 'The game was exciting to watch.') Tj T*
(- Ambiguous context: Assess claims in relation to user query and location.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
