(3.0 Researching Claims and Evidence) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assessors must search for reputable external evidence before making a rating decision.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hierarchy of Source Quality:) Tj T*
(1. Primary / Authoritative Sources: Official government portals \(.gov, .gov.br\), international organizations \(WHO, UN, NASA, NOAA\), official sports leagues \(FIFA, NHL, NBA\), and academic peer-reviewed institutions.) Tj T*
(2. Reputable Secondary Sources: Established news agencies \(Reuters, AP News, BBC\), major encyclopedias, and recognized educational platforms.) Tj T*
(3. Low Quality / Unverifiable: Social media posts, user forums, anonymous blogs, and uncorroborated marketing sites.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evidence must directly confirm or refute the specific entity and predicate in the claim.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
