(4.0 Factuality Rating Scale) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assign one of the six standard ratings:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Accurate: The claim is confirmed by reputable and authoritative evidence.) Tj T*
(- Inaccurate: The claim is contradicted by reputable and authoritative evidence.) Tj T*
(- Unsupported: The claim asserts a verifiable fact, but thorough search reveals no reliable corroboration.) Tj T*
(- Disputed: Authoritative sources directly disagree on the fact with no prevailing consensus.) Tj T*
(- Can't confidently assess: Available evidence is inaccessible, contradictory without resolution, or insufficient.) Tj T*
(- No claims present: The sentence contains solely opinions, recommendations, greetings, or non-factual text.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
